# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The TCT run-cache is a HASH-CHAINED EVIDENCE STORE, not text.
#
# Every record carries prev_sha = sha256 of the previous record's raw LINE.
# This repo is checked out with core.autocrlf=true, so committing these files
# without the marker below makes git rewrite every line ending to CRLF on the
# next checkout or branch switch. The bytes change, every hash after line 1
# stops matching, and verification-gate.sh reports the chain as
# "BROKEN/tampered" — indistinguishable from someone actually forging it.
#
# That happened on 2026-09-11: tct-run-test.sh verify-chain said OK, the
# files were committed, three branch switches followed, and the Stop hook
# then rejected four passing features. Restoring LF made the chain verify
# again, which proved the records were intact and git was the culprit.
#
# THE PRIMARY FIX IS .gitignore, NOT THIS FILE. init-project.sh excludes
# .claude/run-cache/ precisely because it is per-machine evidence signed by a
# per-machine .chain-secret — this project predates that block, so the
# directory was tracked and got normalised. It is untracked now. The rule
# below is defence in depth for anyone who re-adds it.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion for these paths. Do not remove
# it, and do not "normalise" this directory.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/run-cache/**    -text

# Keep the manifest byte-stable too: spec-hash-guard and manifest-state-gate
# both hash file contents, and a CRLF rewrite would move those hashes.
.claude/feature-manifest.json   -text
.claude/specs/**/spec.md        -text
